---
// Plain-language privacy policy (PIPEDA). Draft copy for Kelly to approve.
// Keep in step with docs/privacy/data-inventory.md and the LJoJ Data Retention
// Policy: any change to what we collect, where it goes or how long we keep it
// updates all three in the same pull request (CLAUDE.md rule 6).
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';

const lastUpdated = 'November 18, 2026';
const privacy = site.email.privacy;
---

<Base title="Privacy" description={`How ${site.name} handles personal information.`}>
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="muted">Last updated {lastUpdated}</p>

  <p>
    We are {site.name}, a small family stationery business. We collect as little personal
    information as we can, and we never sell it. This page explains what we collect, why, where it
    goes and how long we keep it.
  </p>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    Our owner, Kelly, is accountable for how we handle personal information. You can reach us about
    privacy at <a href={`mailto:${privacy}`}>{privacy}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Visiting this website</h2>
  <p>
    This website has no forms, no accounts, no cookies, no ads and no tracking or analytics scripts.
    Every file comes from our own domain.
  </p>
  <p>
    To show you the site and protect it from abuse, our hosting provider, Cloudflare, processes
    basic technical information about each visit: your IP address, browser type, the page you asked
    for, the time, and the page that linked you here. We don't keep logs of individual visits. We
    see only overall statistics, such as how many visits the site had.
  </p>

  <h2>Emailing us</h2>
  <p>
    If you email one of our addresses, we receive your name, email address and whatever you write.
    We use it only to reply to you. Our email runs on Google Workspace.
  </p>

  <h2>Buying from us at a market</h2>
  <p>
    Card payments are handled by Square. We don't see or keep your full card number. If you ask for
    a receipt by email or text, Square uses your email address or phone number to send it. We keep
    records of our sales because tax law requires it.
  </p>

  <h2>Instagram</h2>
  <p>
    We link to our Instagram account but don't embed it on this site. If you message us on
    Instagram, Meta handles that message under its own privacy policy.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    This website is for adults. We don't knowingly collect personal information from children. The
    artwork on our cards is made by our own kids, and we never share their faces, full names, ages,
    schools or where they live.
  </p>

  <h2>Who handles your information</h2>
  <p>
    We use a few service providers. Each one processes information only to provide its service to
    us. Some store or process information outside Canada, where it may be subject to the laws of
    those countries.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts and protects this website (mainly the United States and
      Europe).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Google Workspace</strong> runs our email (may be outside Canada).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Square</strong> processes card payments at markets.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Meta</strong> runs Instagram, if you contact us there.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Information</th>
          <th scope="col">How long</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Website visit details</td>
          <td>We keep none. Cloudflare processes them only to serve and protect the site.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Emails you send us</td>
          <td>24 months after our last message with you, unless they are part of an order.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Privacy requests and complaints</td>
          <td>Until resolved and any appeal is finished, then 24 months.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Sales records</td>
          <td>6 years from the end of the tax year, as tax law requires.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>When we no longer need information, we delete it.</p>

  <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask to see the personal information we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or withdraw
    your consent for us to use it. Email <a href={`mailto:${privacy}`}>{privacy}</a>. We will reply
    within 30 days. We may ask you to confirm who you are first.
  </p>

  <h2>Keeping it safe</h2>
  <p>
    We protect our accounts with two-factor authentication, give access only to people who need it,
    and use secure connections (HTTPS) for this website. If a privacy breach could cause you
    significant harm, we will tell you and report it to the Office of the Privacy Commissioner of
    Canada.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions or concerns</h2>
  <p>
    Please contact us first at <a href={`mailto:${privacy}`}>{privacy}</a>, and we will do our best
    to help. If you are not satisfied, you can complain to the
    <a href="https://www.priv.gc.ca/en/report-a-concern/">
      Office of the Privacy Commissioner of Canada
    </a>
    .
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this page</h2>
  <p>
    If we change how we handle personal information, we will update this page and the date at the
    top.
  </p>
</Base>
